<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> An Environmental Project</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How Can We Help the Environment?</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Reading: reading_1: Infer meaning from context clues in short texts.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">reading_2: Write responses to questions about informational texts.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">phonemic_awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by segmenting multisyllabic words into syllables.</li>
            </p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Reading: Can infer meanings of environmental vocabulary from context (e.g., 'Go green means protecting nature.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can write reflections on environmental informative text by answering key questions and sharing their thoughts (e.g., 'What was the story about?' 'It was about saving water.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can segment multisyllabic words into syllables, demonstrating knowledge of phonemic awareness (e.g., dividing 'presentation' into 'pre-sen-ta-tion').</li>
            </p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of the lesson's core vocabulary and concepts related to the theme "How Can We Help the Environment?".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of different environmental actions (e.g., planting trees, cleaning a park, recycling bottles, watering plants). Students look at the pictures and the teacher asks, "What do you see?" and "How can we help our environment?". Students share ideas using vocabulary like 'plant', 'clean', 'care'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary from the previous lesson and words related to the environmental actions shown in the pictures (e.g., 'project', 'plant', 'environment', 'care'). The teacher also models how to infer meaning by pointing to a picture and saying, "This boy is putting paper in the blue bin. This means he will 'recycle' paper." The teacher models the pronunciation of 'will' /wɪl/ and 'I'll' /aɪl/ by giving simple sentences: "I will plant a tree." "I'll clean the classroom."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we 'care' for plants, what do we do? (A) Water them. (B) Break them." (Target: 'care')</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is a 'project'? Is it a small job or a big plan?" (Target: 'project')</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to the scenario "An Environmental Project," focusing on reading comprehension.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informational text (e.g., a notice or a blog post excerpt) titled "Our Green School Project" about a school's environmental activities. The text includes specific vocabulary (project, environment, classroom, plan, garden, trees, plants, meeting, present, grow, clean, care, excited, local) and grammar (Present simple for everyday events: "We wash the plastic and glass bottles every day."; Future simple for plans: "We will plant trees tomorrow."; Imperatives for instructions: "Bring a shovel to the park.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will be able to understand the main idea and specific details in short, simple informational texts related to environmental topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher distributes the text. Students read silently.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b> "What is the text about?" "What is the school doing?" (Students answer orally or by pointing to key words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read sentences about the text and mark them True or False (e.g., "The students will plant flowers." T/F).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match phrases (e.g., "clean the park") with specific days or times mentioned in the text (e.g., "Saturday morning").</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on reading comprehension, vocabulary recognition, and phonemic awareness.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice inferring meaning from context clues, identifying future plans using the future simple, understanding instructions using imperatives, describing everyday events with present simple, and segmenting multisyllabic words from the text. Focus on vocabulary: 'project', 'environment', 'classroom', 'plan', 'garden', 'trees', 'plants', 'clean', 'care', 'participate', 'excited'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Vocabulary from Context (Controlled Practice):</b> Teacher provides sentences directly from the "Our Green School Project" text with key vocabulary words removed. Students choose the correct word from a box to complete the sentences. Example: "We _______ a special project for our school." (Options: clean, have, plant).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Inferring Meaning (Semi-controlled):</b> The teacher highlights specific phrases or sentences from the text containing vocabulary words (e.g., "Go green means protecting nature." or "We are 'excited' about the upcoming event."). Students work in pairs to discuss and write down what they think the highlighted words or phrases mean, using context clues. Teacher circulates, guiding and providing feedback.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Phonemic Awareness & Sentence Reading (Pair Check):</b> The teacher writes multisyllabic words from the text on the board (e.g., 'presentation', 'environment', 'participate', 'classroom'). The teacher models segmenting each word into syllables (e.g., "en-vi-ron-ment", "par-ti-ci-pate"). Students then work in pairs to segment other words. After, students read key sentences from the text aloud to their partner, focusing on the pronunciation of 'will' /wɪl/ and 'I'll' /aɪl/, and identifying sentences with future plans, instructions, or everyday events.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students use the language in a realistic scenario: "An Environmental Project," demonstrating reading comprehension and ability to respond to informational texts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Written responses to questions about the informational text. Students will individually read a slightly modified version of "Our Green School Project" text (with one or two new details or slightly rephrased sentences) and answer comprehension and reflective questions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher distributes the modified text and a worksheet with questions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the text independently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then write answers to questions that require them to:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify main ideas and specific details (e.g., "What will the students do on Saturday?").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Infer meaning from context (e.g., "What does 'upcoming event' mean in the text?").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Formulate simple reflections on the information (e.g., "Why is this project important for our environment?").</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Encourage the use of target grammar (present simple, future simple, imperatives) and vocabulary from the lesson in their responses.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of students' reading comprehension and ability to infer meaning and respond to texts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during the production task and review of written responses using a simple checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' written answers to the comprehension and reflection questions from the Production stage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy of answers related to the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to infer meaning from context (e.g., correctly explaining 'Go green').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'project', 'environment', 'plant', 'clean', 'care').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and completeness of written responses (even with simple sentences).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today I learned that the story was about _______."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I understand better is _______, it means _______."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson and preparation for the next stage in the learning sequence.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy for me when reading the text today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was difficult for me, and what can I do next time to understand better?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The students showed good progress in inferring meaning and identifying key information. The phonemic awareness activity on segmenting multisyllabic words helped some students with decoding longer vocabulary words. Some students still need more practice writing complete sentences. I will need to provide sentence starters or frames for the next writing task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction), students will actively use the environmental vocabulary and grammar to discuss and propose actions for their own "Environmental Project" in pairs, building on the comprehension of the informational text.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>